Running the assistant downloads and uses other models and libraries under their
own terms. Two of them matter before you use this in anything other than a
personal project:

- XTTS v2 (Coqui) is downloaded on first launch. Its weights are under the
  Coqui Public Model License (CPML), which is non-commercial:
  https://tts-hub.github.io/cpml
  main.py sets COQUI_TOS_AGREED so that download can proceed. That accepts the
  CPML for the voice model. It does not relicense the weights.

- The language-model file models/Qwen3-8B-Q5_K_M.gguf is not in this
  repository. The Qwen3-8B-GGUF weights published by Qwen are under Apache-2.0:
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-8B-GGUF

faster-whisper, CTranslate2, llama.cpp, and the other Python packages keep
their own licenses.
